<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:30Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>US bans Canadian alcohol, motorcycles and dairy products as trade spat escalates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5090219c28e30edf2fc43b4959293ecab722e4fd4abb97d0986f060e44d6e150</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T02:36:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-us-bans-canadian-alcohol-motorcycles-and-dairy-products-as-trade-spat-escalates--c7ae8aea47d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-us-bans-canadian-alcohol-motorcycles-and-dairy-products-as-trade-spat-escalates" /><summary type="html">The US and Canada escalated a bitter trade dispute on Tuesday, with Washington imposing new import bans on Canadian alcohol, motorcycles and dairy products as Ottawa's retaliatory tariffs on US goods took effect.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Key post-9/11 air toxicity information was kept secret for 25 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd73a4018c5ff31d8465e315c911f9a580557b9b110c3b86ae8961d26a65aaa3</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T01:44:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-key-post-9-11-air-toxicity-information-was-kept-secret-for-25-years--591bfaa53874.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-key-post-9-11-air-toxicity-information-was-kept-secret-for-25-years" /><summary type="html">New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani released tens of thousands of previously undisclosed documents on Tuesday detailing what city officials knew about toxic air after the September 11 attacks, as the 25th anniversary approaches and thousands continue to suffer from related illnesses.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Smithsonian chief Lonnie Bunch steps down amid Trump administration pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c1df705be601c660337b921d41209501df153058ebbb3184dbb8797a7951bac</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T00:10:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-smithsonian-chief-lonnie-bunch-steps-down-amid-trump-administration-pressure--786389f668db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-smithsonian-chief-lonnie-bunch-steps-down-amid-trump-administration-pressure" /><summary type="html">The Smithsonian announced Tuesday that Secretary Lonnie Bunch will leave his post at the end of the year, as the institution faces continued scrutiny from the Trump administration over how its museums present US history.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East live: US destroys five Iranian oil tankers as Iran threatens Kuwait and Bahrain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f3455c387973ca2fe8060891624b50830984ea52b4638398e39f1c79ac5aaff</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T23:07:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-middle-east-live-us-destroys-five-iranian-oil-tankers-as-iran-threatens-kuwait-and-bahrain--06fb925ebc76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-middle-east-live-us-destroys-five-iranian-oil-tankers-as-iran-threatens-kuwait-and-bahrain" /><summary type="html">US forces destroyed five Iranian oil carriers on Tuesday after Tehran launched ballistic missiles at an American warship twice in recent days. Iran also launched strikes on US targets in Jordan, and threatened attacks on oil tankers off Kuwait and Bahrain. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>‘Was this a state visit?’ Indian opposition leader raises serious questions over Paris BAPS temple</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:208e3ca5193b9834065f8291fd41521cbd0623af683a645cf55ff1f32b5cb3db</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T22:43:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260908-was-this-a-state-visit-indian-opposition-leader-raises-serious-questions-over-paris-baps-te--252ccf567093.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260908-was-this-a-state-visit-indian-opposition-leader-raises-serious-questions-over-paris-baps-temple" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Anish Gawande. He sees the controversy surrounding the inauguration of the BAPS temple near Paris as more than an isolated dispute over the treatment of female staff at the Eiffel Tower. From his perspective, the incident exposes a broader and insufficiently scrutinized intersection of religion, diplomacy, political power, labor practices, and diaspora politics. At the center of his argument is an ambiguity over the boundary between private religious and state-sanctioned activity.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Mourinho's Real Madrid edge Inter Milan in Champions League opener</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df132172350587b3ea966bc33146e5b28e75651be07d43042ca4f4de07c71cfa</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T21:23:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20260908-mourinho-real-madrid-edge-inter-milan-in-champions-league-opener--acf85acfd7a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260908-mourinho-real-madrid-edge-inter-milan-in-champions-league-opener" /><summary type="html">Jose Mourinho's Real Madrid began their Champions League campaign with a 2-1 win over his former side Inter Milan on Tuesday, taking a two-goal lead before Carlos Augusto pulled one back. Thibaut Courtois and Inter goalkeeper Josep Martinez both made crucial saves as Madrid held on for victory at the Santiago Bernabeu.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>UK, France, ⁠Canada sanction Israeli West Bank goods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50e91bd1c6cce31598bcaf33023c20a4ef6d39818ab36542fba1f7ce692fe7e5</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T21:02:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260908-uk-france-canada-sanction-israeli-west-bank-goods--fdacae129b44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260908-uk-france-canada-sanction-israeli-west-bank-goods" /><summary type="html">Israel said on Tuesday it was closing Britain's consulate in East Jerusalem in response to plans by the UK, France and Canada to block imports from Israeli settlements in the West Bank. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Julie Norman, Associate Fellow with the Middle East and North Africa Programme at Chatham House and Director of UCL’s Israel-Palestine Initiative.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Accelerating diversification: Canada seeks economic sovereignty amid Trump's 'nonsensical' posturing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5bd1082d6ae31d89876a6cfdd3c7fe131dde0b7f2ea82ca9cd8629189dc69d8e</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T21:02:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260908-accelerating-diversification-canada-seeks-economic-sovereignty-amid-trump-s-nonsensical-pos--b741b10ffed3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260908-accelerating-diversification-canada-seeks-economic-sovereignty-amid-trump-s-nonsensical-posturing" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Jean Simard, President and CEO of the Aluminum Association of Canada. According to Simard, the US-Canada aluminum dispute is not your conventional disagreement over trade, but rather a 'Trump posture that makes no sense". As American industrial demand substantially exceeds domestic production capacity, tariffs will do nothing to reduce Canadian aluminum from the US market. Protectionism does not eliminate interdependence, explains Simard, it makes that interdependence considerably more expensive.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya cracks down on foreign traders</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd4857f1c7a54fbc6c32292ed0ee5d0f9ea7fd22cec0930d9f4a89f9a497015d</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T20:29:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kenya-cracks-down-on-foreign-traders--c31b8c5d613f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-cracks-down-on-foreign-traders" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Hundreds of Burundians flocked to ⁠their embassy in ​Nairobi to get travel documents to return home. Also, in his first speech to the National assembly, Senegal’s Prime Minister Ahmadou Al Aminou Lo slams the rise of xenophobic rhetoric on the continent. And I speak to the founder of an AI surgical non-profit of the work being done in Tanzania to extend the reach of the country's 27 over burdened neurosurgeons.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Paris probes why women staff removed from Eiffel Tower for Hindu visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db621461a57a80bd915389d179eb48cac00e1242c6af7ab283eb197889f4eccd</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T20:19:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/paris-probes-why-women-staff-removed-from-eiffel-tower-for-hindu-visit--d7222b3ac409.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/paris-probes-why-women-staff-removed-from-eiffel-tower-for-hindu-visit" /><summary type="html">The mayor of Paris on Tuesday ordered investigations over the removal of women staff at the Eiffel Tower during a visit by a Hindu religious group which prompted an employee walkout and the one-day closure of the monument. The Eiffel Tower, which says it receives nearly seven million people a year, reopened on Tuesday morning after a furore resulted in the landmark being shut down on Monday. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports</summary></entry><entry><title>Canada PM stands his ground as Ottawa's retaliatory tariffs on US goods take effect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b2f1908b7d5847f695401ff91d8e0f80d7d9db675f2574ba0baea58adce35aa</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T20:11:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260908-canada-pm-stands-his-ground-as-ottawa-s-retaliatory-tariffs-on-us-goods-take-effect--5257aa9e0f28.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260908-canada-pm-stands-his-ground-as-ottawa-s-retaliatory-tariffs-on-us-goods-take-effect" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney said it was a shame that trade talks with the US collapsed but that he would continue to fight to protect Canada's sovereignty, as his government's promised counter-tariffs on $20 billion worth of US exports took effect. Also in the segment, Cuba says economic damage from decades of US trade embargo has risen to a record $8 billion.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Trump posts AI map showing US 'takeover' of North America, Iceland and Caribbean</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:998cf4a3c64718f4e18181c1adf1b501f2862bb679e15d4cf4886b108afb6cc2</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T19:43:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-posts-ai-map-showing-us-takeover-of-north-america-iceland-and-caribbean-1--323e2c877033.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-posts-ai-map-showing-us-takeover-of-north-america-iceland-and-caribbean-1" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump shared an AI-generated map Monday appearing to show the US absorbing Canada, Mexico, Greenland, Iceland, Cuba and parts of the Caribbean into a giant “United States of America”. Shared with no context, the post sparked diplomatic backlash with Iceland summoning its ambassador and Mexico reiterating its sovereignty. Denmark also pushed back over Greenland. Online, the map has triggered widespread ridicule and questions about Trump’s fitness for office.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>'Europe's museums are under siege', art recovery expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:534fd1659fe2a760dcdde301dc1fbe8726702b2fd743806bf3bdcc51aa0a2c71</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T19:39:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-s-museums-are-under-siege-art-recovery-expert-says--a6c568de478c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-s-museums-are-under-siege-art-recovery-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Two thieves sliced through a fence, climbed through a window and stole four valuable Renoir paintings Tuesday from a small museum on the French Riviera, but abandoned two of the artworks as they fled, authorities said. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Christopher Marinello, a lawyer and founder of Art Recovery International. He says that offering a reward for information could go a long way in recovering stolen artworks.</summary></entry><entry><title>Canada will move faster from US reliance as tariffs take effect and Trump response looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0fd19f9d34dfce543661544cc65c7237cb60e7f8d2b6589a1b8864c4e1dfe78</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T19:19:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/canada-will-move-faster-from-us-reliance-as-tariffs-take-effect-and-trump-response-looms--f0cf636eb7a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/canada-will-move-faster-from-us-reliance-as-tariffs-take-effect-and-trump-response-looms" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney said Tuesday that Canada would move faster to reduce its economic reliance on the United States as retaliatory tariffs took effect on about $20 billion worth of U.S. goods and the country braced for President Donald Trump’s response. FRANCE 24's Christopher Guly reports from Ottawa.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump tells Putin he wants swift end to Ukraine war, Kremlin says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5363fe06e80071821f32bee7019fc0ce99d5572c5178e2709bf2c37a07bc2460</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T19:07:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-trump-tells-putin-he-wants-swift-end-to-ukraine-war-kremlin-says--5f2aae4d01c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-trump-tells-putin-he-wants-swift-end-to-ukraine-war-kremlin-says" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump told Russian President Vladimir Putin he wanted a swift end to the Ukraine war, the Kremlin said, arguing that peace could pave the way for a broad restoration of US-Russia ties. The hour-long call Tuesday followed weekend talks by US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner in Moscow and Kyiv to try to revive stalled peace efforts.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French police hunt Renoir thieves after lightning museum heist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:254bbbba4993d728dbb60e5b96163929cc9f7804108657a77b661558d367a19b</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:35:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-police-hunt-renoir-thieves-after-lightning-museum-heist--2421572c17c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-police-hunt-renoir-thieves-after-lightning-museum-heist" /><summary type="html">French police on Tuesday hunted for two thieves who escaped with two Renoir paintings from a museum, after abandoning two others as they fled, in a burglary that reignited concerns about the protection of France's cultural heritage. The heist is the latest in a string of such robberies including the daylight theft last year of crown jewellery valued at around $100 million from the Louvre in Paris. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu under fire over report UAE warned of October 7 attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a025965adfd0c3fac1004712ae1a3fb6543d03f3e76e3837e9d7c9e4b8a534eb</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:31:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-under-fire-over-report-uae-warned-of-october-7-attack--7fd6213c811c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-under-fire-over-report-uae-warned-of-october-7-attack" /><summary type="html">Israeli opposition leaders on Tuesday called Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu unfit to serve after a report that the United Arab Emirates had warned him before the October 7, 2023 Hamas attack. Haaretz newspaper, in a report excerpted from a forthcoming book by its reporters, said UAE President Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan spoke to Netanyahu a week and a half before the attack and told him that Hamas was planning a major operation. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK, France, Canada to ban imports from Israeli settlements</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:148aae411065a364feafc37bbf5a168cd434985134d71a866d9d95d0d88ee2a4</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:24:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/uk-france-canada-to-ban-imports-from-israeli-settlements--5103789d99a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/uk-france-canada-to-ban-imports-from-israeli-settlements" /><summary type="html">Britain, France and Canada said Tuesday they will ban imports from Israeli settlements in the occupied West Bank, with a UK minister accusing Israel of turning a blind eye to the "ethnic cleansing" of Palestinians there. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Missiles or mediation? Trump envoys shuttle between Russia and Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49758df68f7e6d57299821c28247f440d05c33fa2491ec2adc16cbb5105e9115</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:19:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260908-missiles-or-mediation-trump-envoys-shuttle-between-russia-and-ukraine--b5fc503da412.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260908-missiles-or-mediation-trump-envoys-shuttle-between-russia-and-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Exactly two months ago, Ukraine’s momentum was all the talk at a Nato summit in Turkey. What with its long-range drones and Donald Trump’s surprise announcement that the US would allow Kyiv to produce Patriot anti-ballistic missiles on home soil. That was then. This is now: Trump's deal's yet to materialize, Russia’s ramped up cruise missile launches and Ukraine’s run out of air defenses to stop them. Moscow's also failing to stop incoming missiles. What happens in war when for both sides, offense proves better than defense?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Messi, Mbappé and Kane headline Ballon d'Or shortlist, Vozinha named for Yashin award</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:001df5e0299d790982aa34df11abbe78d8373665f262690f2e8cdf8eb2447d11</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T17:52:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20260908-messi-mbappe-kane-headline-ballon-d-or-shortlist-vozinha-named-yashin-award--aa1e205f4849.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260908-messi-mbappe-kane-headline-ballon-d-or-shortlist-vozinha-named-yashin-award" /><summary type="html">Eight-time laureate Lionel Messi is in the 30-man shortlist for the 2026 Men's Ballon ​d'Or, with Harry Kane and Kylian Mbappé among the favourites to succeed France's Ousmane Dembélé. Cape Verde's Vozinha has been shortlisted for the goalkeepers' Yashin Trophy after his heroics at the recent World Cup.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>'US Midterm elections tend to be referendums on the unpopularity of the president'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fb885690846eb25505b0cebf3d740526641751bf79153bc548e21155c2a7211</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T16:25:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterm-elections-tend-to-be-referendums-on-the-unpopularity-of-the-president--66d8de516e55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterm-elections-tend-to-be-referendums-on-the-unpopularity-of-the-president" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome Michelle Swers, Professor of Government at Georgetown University. She frames the New Hampshire primary as both a major Senate contest and an unusually strong indication of the national political climate ahead of November. While Democrats face a difficult Senate map and cannot afford to surrender an open seat they already hold, the broader midterm political environment might become a referendum on President Donald Trump’s performance. New Hampshire is particularly instructive because its closely divided electorate makes national political currents more visible. Swers argues that Trump’s low approval and the local economic consequences of tariffs on Canada create significant headwinds for Republicans, especially in a state whose political identity is strongly associated with resistance to taxation.</summary></entry><entry><title>US war on Iran: 'Incompetent administration when it comes to negotiations and prosecuting war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1fe969981bdba177208a2ddcc85c25fc6a517f2af1aa674404234e15163ab9b</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T16:16:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war--1e3a59faed45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war" /><summary type="html">Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Simpson Center. She frames the war in the Persian Gulf as a mutually damaging stalemate in which neither Washington nor Tehran has found a politically sustainable exit: "There are no winners in this war". Her central argument is that the conflict has created a problem of face-saving as much as military strategy. The US faces rising economic and electoral costs, while Iran confronts shortages, inflation, domestic dissent and intensified repression. Neither side, in her assessment, can plausibly claim success.</summary></entry><entry><title>The 'Brenaissance': Brendan Fraser on 'Pressure', winning an Oscar in 'The Whale' and 'The Mummy 4'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ad32ce95626eb09b4b4bb3ec1b40dffe7dd4745c9839f9f6bcb5539e49ceb51</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T15:55:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260908-the-brenaissance-brendan-fraser-on-pressure-winning-an-oscar-in-the-whale-and-the-mummy-4--cb50a0661961.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260908-the-brenaissance-brendan-fraser-on-pressure-winning-an-oscar-in-the-whale-and-the-mummy-4" /><summary type="html">From "The Mummy" to his Oscar-winning performance in "The Whale", Brendan Fraser's career has taken some extraordinary turns. At the Deauville American Film Festival, he talks to Eve Jackson about his "Brenaissance", playing General Dwight D. Eisenhower in "Pressure", what D-Day can teach us about the dangers of ignoring science and his return as Rick O'Connell in "The Mummy 4".</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry></feed>
